sequenceDiagram
    participant C as Customer
    participant J as Java application
    participant R as MRS
    participant D as MySQL
    Note over J,R: Authenticated sessions already established.<br/>Java binds ownerHex using customer /whoami.
    rect rgb(235, 244, 253)
        Note over C,D: 1. Propose — model tools use only the customer client
        C->>J: Ask to cancel order 1003
        J->>R: Customer token: POST /requestCancellation
        R->>D: Inject customer principal, call request_cancellation
        D-->>R: PENDING request UUID<br/>Order unchanged
        R-->>J: Pending result
    end
    rect rgb(244, 244, 244)
        Note over C,D: 2. Review — trusted terminal path, outside model dispatch
        C->>J: /confirm UUID
        J->>R: Customer token: GET /requests/UUID
        R-->>J: Owned request: order, reason, state
        J-->>C: Display stored request and confirmation challenge
        C->>J: Type exact CONFIRM UUID
        J->>R: Customer token: re-fetch request
        R-->>J: Owned request, Java checks order and reason
    end
    rect rgb(235, 247, 239)
        Note over C,D: 3. Confirm — trusted terminal path uses the executor client
        J->>R: Executor token: POST /confirmCancellation<br/>(requestId, ownerHex)
        R->>D: Inject executor principal, call confirm_cancellation
        Note over R,D: Check executor and owner binding.<br/>Lock order before request.<br/>Validate state, expiry and version.<br/>Commit cancellation and audit.
        D-->>R: CONFIRMED result
        R-->>J: Confirmed result
        J-->>C: Structured outcome
    end
    Note over J,R: Both clients share one process.<br/>The model's tools never receive the executor client.
